<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nabeshima Naoshige</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1538">1538</a>–<a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nabeshima Naoshige was a Japanese warlord of Hizen province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>. A leading retainer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryuzoji-clan">Ryuzoji clan</a>, he took effective control of its lands after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryuzoji-takanobu">Ryuzoji Takanobu</a> was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-okitanawate">Battle of Okitanawate</a> in 1584. Recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and then the Tokugawa, his family ruled Saga Domain until the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nabeshima-naoshige.jpg" alt="Nabeshima Naoshige" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miura Shisan 三浦子サン (?–1794) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nabeshima_Naoshige_by_Miura_Shisan_(Chokokan)_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
